#
# Counter-example for math:IncompleteConfidenceIntervalShape (Rule I4): a
# math:ConfidenceInterval carrying its two bounds through math:hasIntervalBound (so the
# sh:minCount 2 bound arm is SATISFIED) but omitting math:confidenceLevel, tripping the
# level arm's sh:minCount 1 — shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval).
# Single violation: it is NOT typed math:CredibleInterval, so math:IntervalKindConflationShape
# (Rule I3) stays satisfied, and its two bounds keep the bound arm satisfied — EXACTLY ONE
# finding, no sibling fires.
# Back-reference: math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Negative counterpart of conformance-fixtures/confidence-interval-complete.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecConfidenceIntervalIncomplete).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:levellessCI a math:ConfidenceInterval ;
    math:hasIntervalBound ex:ciLower , ex:ciUpper .    # bounds present, but NO math:confidenceLevel

ex:ciLower a math:MathematicalObject .
ex:ciUpper a math:MathematicalObject .
